d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d83cabb0-45f8-5769-8a35-16968ddc61ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-63242" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c334d2f47b36ac6d7ca620e044afda648aafa13ad9559af5131a50d2768d439.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "There is an **open** circle at $x=\\frac{3}{4},$ and the red arrow starts from $\\frac{3}{4}$ and goes to the **left**. This indicates that $x$ should consist of all the values **less than ** $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x<\\frac{3}{4}.$"}]}
